{
  "assembly_notes": "Round gateleg drop-leaf table. One rigid table_frame root carries the fixed centre spine of the top, the steel carcass under it and every support pivot. Two drop_leaf parts are REVOLUTE children of the frame, hinged on both long edges of the spine; q=0 is raised and coplanar with the spine, q=upper is folded straight down beside the frame. Because the leaves hang on the hinge line and every support swings out well outboard of it, no support and no folded leaf ever share space. support_build is one structural family of swing-out leaf supports pivoting on a vertical axis in the frame: swing_gate, arc_gate, cross_trestle, telescoping_brace (which adds a real prismatic lock), wall_bracket and latch_gate (which adds a pivoting latch). frame_build changes what fills and carries the carcass: open_spine, shelf_spine, double_shelf, caster_glide (swivel plus roll axes per caster) and brake_caster (which adds a pivoting brake pedal per caster). support_per_leaf multiplies the support stations on each side, always symmetric, so the model carries 2 * support_per_leaf support parts. top_diameter_m, spine_width_ratio and table_height_m are the independent parameters; palette, grain grooves and fastener counts are non-core. foot_build is what the frame stands on, independent of what fills it: fixed_glide keeps the frame on small rubber glides, pad_foot spreads the load on broad pads with a steel plate, and swivel_caster / braked_caster lift the whole frame by one caster radius onto four casters, each with a vertical swivel over a rolling wheel and, for braked_caster, a brake pedal that swings onto the tyre. The frame derives its floor lift from the foot candidate, so every frame_build combines with every foot_build.",
